  "description": "T3-Lime(Tilia cordata)-nearest gate\r-reduce crown to previous points of reduction retain 10% fine furnishings for crown continuity\r\rT4-Lime(Tilia cordata)-larger tree  \r-reduce crown to previous points of reduction retain 10% fine furnishings for crown continuity\r\rT5-Olive(Oleo europaea)-leaning inbound over lawn\r-cut back all stems by 40%(1.8m) to suitable growth points\r-remove all deadwood branches\r\rRear LH corner\r(T6 & T7) 2x Cypress(Cupressus)-both dead/leaning\r-fell both trees to ground level\r\rLH boundary-nearest house\r(T8) -Crab Apple(Malus sylvestris)\r-reduce length of all long 'leggy' branches by up to 1.2m to good growth points\r\rIN NEIGHBOURING PROPERTY\r(T9) - Robinia(R.pseudoplatanus)\r-reduce all overhanging branches by up to 2.5m to good growth points\r-remove all overhanging deadwood branches\r\rAll works to T3, T4, T5, T8 & T9 are for routine maintenance. \rWorks to T6 & T7 are due to the trees being in dead and leaning.",
